<p>On Monday, Apple announced <a href="https://www.apple.com/newsroom/2026/11/apple-reports-fourth-quarter-results/">record fourth-quarter earnings</a>, with total revenue of $114.5B, up 12 percent from the year-ago quarter. iPhone revenue was up 17.5%, Mac revenue was up 23.7%, and Services revenue was up 9.8%. Wearables revenue was down 7.9% and iPad revenue was down 10.4%.</p>
<p>Beginning at 2pm Pacific, Apple execs will spend an hour on the phone with financial industry analysts. We&#8217;ll have our usual transcript. It&#8217;ll be the first earnings call for John Ternus as CEO.</p>
